cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, please cite the paper."
title: "Regime-Dependent Rebalancing: A Data-Driven, Non-Invasive Framework for Long-Tailed, Scale-Variant Object Detection in UAV Imagery"
type: article
authors:
  - name: "AirAI-Lab"
journal: "IEEE Transactions on Geoscience and Remote Sensing"
year: 2026
notes: "Under review"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AirAI-Lab/DAHP-UAV-Detection"
abstract: >-
  A label-only profiler quantifies long-tail, scale imbalance, and confusion
  pathologies in UAV imagery and maps them, through a regime-dependent
  rebalancing law, to strictly non-invasive training-time policies.
keywords:
  - UAV object detection
  - long-tailed recognition
  - data-driven profiling
  - oversampling
  - VisDrone
  - UAVDT
license: MIT
